cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "voynich_xc: Structural Visibility, Pharmaceutical Supply Chains, and Falsifiable Grammar Discovery in the Voynich Manuscript"
message: "If you use this software, lexicon dataset, or synthesis report in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "probablyapigeon"
repository-code: "https://github.com"
url: "https://github.com/blob/main/VOYNICH_CODEX_REPORT.md"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible suite of 35 computational probes built on the XEMBRA (.xc) morpho-syntactic
  interpreter analyzing the 15th-century Voynich Manuscript. Identifies 135 verified
  Pharmaceutical Jar-to-Starred Recipe bridge compounds (voynich_master_lexicon.json/.csv)
  across all six codicological sections and reconstructs all 359 Starred Recipe cards
  (voynich_reconstructed_codex.json) with 100% lexical coverage.
keywords:
  - Voynich Manuscript
  - Computational Linguistics
  - Historical Pharmacy
  - Codicology
  - Morpho-Syntactic Analysis
  - XEMBRA
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
